  "_comment": "VB3-16: the stable field id ledger for the interchange contract's five schemas (schemas/interchange/*.schema.json). One flat name -> id namespace shared by every schema file: the SAME field name always carries the SAME id everywhere it appears with the same meaning (authority, lifecycle, valid_from, valid_to, observed_at, ingested_at, verified_at, recorded_at, occurred_at, ref, status all recur this way). An id is minted once, in the order a field was first introduced, and is NEVER reused: a field that is later removed keeps its row here with status 'deprecated' instead of the id being handed to something new, and a rename is expressed as a brand new id for the new name plus 'deprecated' on the old one, never a reassignment. tools/bm_vault_interchange.py's evolve command and tools/test_bm_vault_interchange.py's registry test both read this file as the single source of truth; every x-field-id embedded in the *.schema.json files must match the id recorded here for that field name.",
